Task 3.3 is the only caller.

**Format decision.** The spec illustrated this column as `"2d ago"` and capped
it at six cells. This plan settles on the compact form — `2d`, `3h`, `12m`,
`5w`, `8mo`, `2y`, and `now` under a minute — capped at **four** cells. The
two cells that buys go to the title, which is the column actually competing
for them in a pane that is only 42% of the terminal. "ago" carries no
information the column position does not.

`now` is a parameter, not `time.Now()` read inside. That is what makes the
function pure and the table below deterministic; it is also the only option
here, since `gochecknoglobals` rules out a package-level clock.

**Boundary rule:** each unit is reported once the duration reaches it, and the
next unit takes over at the point where the smaller one would need three
digits. Weeks stop at 52, after which years apply — so nothing ever exceeds
four cells (`11mo` is the widest).

